WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.768
-...the scope of exactly how far
country music reaches,

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:03.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause you're
a West Virginia guy.

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:04.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-You live in Tennessee.

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:05.772
But you go -- you actually tour
in Europe.

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:08.208
You go to places -- You're going
to Scandinavia? Or...

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:09.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We were just in Sweden...
-Just got --

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:11.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...and Norway, which is...
-Okay, gotcha.

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:14.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's so much fun for me
because I'm exotic...

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:15.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...over there. I'm the...

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:19.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm the definition
of "not exotic" in America.

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:20.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's true.
Nobody says, like,

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, that's
an interesting-looking..."

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:23.156 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right.

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:24.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"...weird thing
I've never seen before."

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:26.159
-Yeah. For them -- They show up,
they've got the hats,

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:28.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
they got chaps.
I mean, they're ready.

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:31.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do they know that nobody
wears chaps over here anymore?

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:32.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. They're not...
-Okay. Gotcha.

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:34.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They think they're doing
the right thing.

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:35.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's fantastic, though,
to go over there

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:36.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause they just seem
to love it.

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:39.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're sort of starved for it
in -- in these countries.

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:41.608 size:88% position:44%
-But also -- They're not
just checking this out

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:43.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
to see what
country music's like.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:44.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
They know...
-No.

00:00:44.244 --> 00:00:46.112
-They're huge fans? They know
the words? They sing along?

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:46.880 line:92%
-They know -- They have --

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
They speak way better English
than my band.

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:50.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:51.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They're -- they're really...
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:53.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean,
it's their second language,

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
but they're better at it
than us.

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:55.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And...

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:57.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, its really impressive.
-They know the words.

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:57.824 line:92%
They -- It's really neat.

00:00:57.824 --> 00:00:59.959
I love going over there
every now and then and...

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:01.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great.
Well, welcome home.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:03.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is also cool.
I always know you --

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:07.400
You're a fan of comedy. You host
the CMAs with Carrie Underwood.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys are great.
-Thank you.

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:10.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Your songs -- A lot of
your songs are really funny.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:14.641
And this is cool that you're
doing this Netflix special.

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:16.309 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Tell us about that.

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:18.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, you know,
it's -- it's interesting.

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:21.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
I love the idea that
between songs

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:23.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
is the challenge for
the musician.

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:24.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know.
-Yeah.

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:25.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You get out there
and it's like --

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:26.386 line:92%
-I learned a long time ago that

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:28.822
if you entertain between songs,
it's gravy.

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:30.023 line:92%
It's like -- People were like,

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:31.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, wow! That was even
entertaining."

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:35.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I really worked on
the comedy chops for a while

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:36.963 line:92%
and started hosting this thing

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:38.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
at our comedy festival
in Nashville

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:40.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
called "The Wild West
Comedy Festival,"

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:42.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
which...that title makes
no sense.

00:01:42.402 --> 00:01:43.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Yeah.
-It's east.

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:46.272
But we had a great time, and
I've got a bunch of comedians.

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:49.109
And we stand up there and --
and tell a bunch of jokes.

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:50.210 line:92%
And Netflix approached and said,

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:52.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Would you like to film that
for a special?"

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:54.581 line:92%
And we did, and it's a blast.

00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:57.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it's also --
I've been at concerts before.

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:57.817 line:92%
I've been to your concerts.

00:01:57.817 --> 00:02:01.421
And there's also that thing of
musicians when they tell a joke,

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:02.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
the audiences...
-Right.

00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:04.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...love them because you're
also a musician.

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:06.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. And that -- Right.
-Like, with comedians,

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:07.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's not -- if you bomb,
you can't say,

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:10.196
"All right, let me get you back
with a song."

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:11.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. Exactly. No.
-Yeah.

00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:14.234
-And it's also the kind of thing
where they buy a ticket

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:15.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
to see music,
and when you're funny,

00:02:15.869 --> 00:02:18.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's just so --
it's so refreshing for them,

00:02:18.605 --> 00:02:19.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
as opposed to if they go
to see you,

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:21.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you're not funny,
they got nothing.

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:22.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Nothing.
-I mean, absolutely...

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:24.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it also makes sense
because I do feel,

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
particularly with you --
and I feel like this is true

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:27.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
of a lot
of country music singers --

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:30.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like
your fan base really...

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:30.917 line:92%
feels like they know you.

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:33.353
Like, there's not a wall
of stardom between the two.

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:35.388
And because they know you,
I think they really like,

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:36.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, this is --
We're actually --

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:38.625
He's telling us jokes. He feels
like he knows us, too."

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:40.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think that's an --
Yeah, it's an important thing

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:43.229
about country music, is we're
not supposed to be the ones

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:44.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
who are way out of touch
and flying around

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:46.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the private jets
and everything,

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:47.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
even though we're completely
out of touch.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:50.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Yeah. [ Laughs ]
-Absolutely.

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:52.639 size:88% position:44%
-You wear a -- You get
a new hat every morning.

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:53.306 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah. Exactly. No.

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:54.674
-You throw it out in the garbage
at the end of the day.

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:56.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I throw it away.
Yeah, no, I can't wearing --

00:02:56.242 --> 00:03:00.046
-You also --
You're really a great lyricist.

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:00.647 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you.

00:03:00.647 --> 00:03:01.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're a fantastic
guitar player.

00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:03.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you got to design
your own guitar this year.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:04.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-This is a Fender?

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:08.054
-Fender recently just came out
with a Brad Paisley Telecaster.

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:09.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great.
So how -- What do they --

00:03:09.556 --> 00:03:13.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you design it, like,
what are they asking you for?

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:14.394 line:92%
Like, what input do you give?

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:16.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You made that sound like
they're crazy...

00:03:16.763 --> 00:03:18.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...for -- for going...

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:19.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I just feel like,
would --

00:03:19.566 --> 00:03:20.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
can you tell them things
that are crazy?

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:23.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What are they asking?
-Are you like, "50 strings!"

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:25.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, what?
-Right.

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:25.805 line:92%
That would be interesting.

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:27.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, that would be good,
right?

00:03:27.073 --> 00:03:28.408 line:92%
-No, basically, they want to --

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:31.544
They want to basically
make something that incorporates

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:33.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
the things you like about
their Teles.

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:34.914 line:92%
-And now is that what you play?

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:35.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that one of the things
you play?

00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:37.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is.
I'm gonna play it tonight.

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:38.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All right. That's great.
That's very exciting.

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.520 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:42.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
We talked about this
on the show,

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:43.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
the first time you were
on the show,

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:44.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
which was the very first week
of the show.

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:46.426 line:92%
We met because you played --

00:03:46.426 --> 00:03:48.061 size:81% position:41%
You were kind enough
to play at my wedding.

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:49.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was, which --
-You played our first dance.

00:03:49.796 --> 00:03:51.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was desperate.
[ Audience "Aws" ]

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.031 line:92%
-It was -- And it was great.

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:53.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my wife,
you surprised my wife.

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:55.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did.
-I knew you were coming.

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:56.302 line:92%
And here's a photo to show

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:57.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
exactly how surprised
my wife was.

00:03:57.637 --> 00:04:00.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
There she is. And, uh...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:02.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was saying this to you
earlier today.

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:05.111
It was heartbreaking 'cause she
had not looked that happy

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:07.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
over the course
of the entire day.

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:07.880 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Yeah. No, she -- Yeah.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:10.483
-I felt like the whole day,
she was looking at me like,

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:11.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Don't blow this."
-Right.

00:04:11.551 --> 00:04:14.654 size:88% position:44%
-And then you showed up,
and it was, like, "Aah!"

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:18.324
-It was really weird for me
because I was approached...

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:19.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know,
what was it, 48 hours?

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:21.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, you were not given
a ton of time.

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:24.397
-I was like, "This is a prank."
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:26.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I was a big fan.
I think you're brilliant,

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:27.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I thought it would be fun
to go do.

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was great.
-And I didn't regret it

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:30.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
one minute.
-And you played

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:31.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
this beautiful song
called "She's Everything."

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:32.505 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I did. I did that.

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:34.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And now I heard you actually
have director's cuts

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:35.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
of some of your songs...
-Yeah.

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:36.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...which are --
you re-write lyrics.

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:39.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
-In the comedy special,
actually. Let me --

00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:40.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
What we have here?
-There you go.

00:04:40.747 --> 00:04:44.517
-One of the things that we --
that I did trying to figure out

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:46.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
what the heck I was gonna
talk about...

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:47.553 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:48.521 line:92%
...was the director's cuts.

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:49.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
director's cuts in movies,

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:52.692
where they have the clips
that didn't make the film.

00:04:52.692 --> 00:04:53.126 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:54.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
-'Cause "She's Everything"
is a very sweet song.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:58.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's a perfect, like,
first dance at a wedding song.

00:04:58.698 --> 00:05:01.334
-But what if there's lines
that are more realistic?

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:03.536
Especially now that you're
married, you'll understand.

00:05:03.536 --> 00:05:06.472
-Okay, got it. So this sort of
the director's cut marriage -

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:08.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right, it's sort of...
-Okay, got it.

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:12.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
♪♪ She's a yellow pair
of runnin' shoes ♪♪

00:05:12.378 --> 00:05:13.913 line:92%
♪♪ A holey pair of jeans ♪♪

00:05:13.913 --> 00:05:16.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
♪♪ She looks great
in cheap sunglasses ♪♪

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:19.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
♪♪ She's a passive-aggressive
little thing ♪♪

00:05:19.719 --> 00:05:20.687 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.687 --> 00:05:23.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
♪♪ She's almost everything
I ever wanted ♪♪

00:05:23.556 --> 00:05:25.525 line:92%
♪♪ Almost everything I need -- ♪♪

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:28.127 size:78% position:39%
You know what I mean?
-Yeah. [ Laughing ]

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:30.396 line:92%
-As opposed to, you know...

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:31.798 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:31.798 --> 00:05:33.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm not quite --
We're not quite there yet.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:34.901 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Right, right, right.

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:37.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's one of the things in
the comedy special that we do,

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
is we dissect
a few of the songs.

00:05:40.206 --> 00:05:42.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, you know, the current
single that I'm doing,

00:05:42.709 --> 00:05:43.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's a few versions
of that as well.

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:45.945
-Well, that's great. Well, I'm
so glad you're sticking around

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:46.846 line:92%
and doing some music for us.

00:05:46.846 --> 00:05:47.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's always great to see you,
buddy.

00:05:47.914 --> 00:05:50.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
-Give it up for Brad Paisley!

